.TH SDL_GetUserFolder 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetUserFolder \- Finds the most suitable user folder for a specific purpose.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_filesystem.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetUserFolder(SDL_Folder folder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Many OSes provide certain standard folders for certain purposes, such as storing pictures, music or videos for a certain user\[char46] This function gives the path for many of those special locations\[char46]
.PP
This function is specifically for _user_ folders, which are meant for the user to access and manage\[char46] For application-specific folders, meant to hold data for the application to manage, see
.BR SDL_GetBasePath ()
and
.BR SDL_GetPrefPath ()\[char46]
.PP
The returned path is guaranteed to end with a path separator (\(aq\(rs\(rs\(aq on Windows, \(aq/\(aq on most other platforms)\[char46]
.PP
If NULL is returned, the error may be obtained with
.BR SDL_GetError ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I folder
the type of folder to find\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns either a null-terminated C string containing the full path to the folder, or NULL if an error happened\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

